From: Hongchan Choi <hongchan@google.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 14:58:35 -0700
Subject: Manage handler lifetime in AudioWorkletMessagingProxy

AudioWorkletMessagingProxy::CreateProcessor posts a task to the
AudioWorklet thread binding a scoped_refptr<AudioWorkletHandler>.
If the main-thread references to AudioWorkletNode and AudioContext are
released while this creation task is in-flight, the handler teardown
could be initiated from the worker thread when the task finishes.

AudioHandler teardown and associated graph structure cleanup are
designed to execute on the main thread.

This CL manages the handler lifetime in AudioWorkletMessagingProxy:
1. AudioWorkletMessagingProxy retains a reference in
   pending_create_processor_handlers_ on the main thread while
   CreateProcessor is pending on the worklet thread.
2. After processor creation completes on the worker thread, a completion
   task DidCreateProcessor transfers the handler reference back to the
   main thread.
3. In DidCreateProcessor and WorkerThreadTerminated, pending handlers
   are released on the main thread under DeferredTaskHandler's graph lock
   to ensure orderly destruction.

